"A1","Heart Failure: Fluid Status Management (Joint Commission)","This learning activity discusses the significant role that fluid management has on the clinical syndrome of heart failure (HF). Key principles of fluid management for hospitalized patients with hypervolemia are presented. This learning activity also describes medications and device therapies used to treat patients with HF experiencing fluid overload. Also discussed is the influence of comorbidities and factors that precipitate hospitalization as they relate to HF as well as the necessary components of patient education. For additional information about patients with heart failure and altered fluid status the learner is encouraged to view the learning activity Heart Failure, Ultrafiltration (Joint Commission Resources).","WKCEConnection"